## Promotion criterion (declared before running)
PROMOTE `supervised` if its encoder linear-probe ≥ 40% (up from ~30%) AND end-to-end proxy val ≥ 10%
(>2.5× the 3.81% control). That would confirm the encoder was the binding ceiling and open room for
the prototype refinements (centered/whitened) to then contribute. Predeclared.

## Rejection/rollback criterion
If linear-probe does NOT rise above ~30% with a supervised client signal, the limiter is elsewhere
